From c33691b81ccf5bea4785af478e3c1fc95b908362 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 15:02:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 05/12] reset: reset-simple: add nexell,s5pxx18-reset

S5P6818 reset controller is one active-low bit per line across 32-bit banks -
reset-simple's active_low mode. Used by GbE, I2C and USB.

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 drivers/reset/reset-simple.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/reset/reset-simple.c b/drivers/reset/reset-simple.c
index 79e94ecfe..6d6fbc247 100644
--- a/drivers/reset/reset-simple.c
+++ b/drivers/reset/reset-simple.c
@@ -148,6 +148,14 @@ static const struct of_device_id reset_simple_dt_ids[] = {
 		.data = &reset_simple_active_low },
 	{ .compatible = "brcm,bcm4908-misc-pcie-reset",
 		.data = &reset_simple_active_low },
+	/*
+	 * Nexell S5P6818 reset controller @0xc0012000: one bit per reset line
+	 * across 32-bit bank registers (bank = id/32, bit = id%32), and a line
+	 * is HELD in reset when its bit is 0 (deassert = set bit) - i.e.
+	 * active-low, exactly reset-simple's active_low mode.
+	 */
+	{ .compatible = "nexell,s5pxx18-reset",
+		.data = &reset_simple_active_low },
 	{ .compatible = "snps,dw-high-reset" },
 	{ .compatible = "snps,dw-low-reset",
 		.data = &reset_simple_active_low },
-- 
